<title>JAPAN: Japan May foreign bond buying at 1.9222 trln yen.</title>
<headline>Japan May foreign bond buying at 1.9222 trln yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net purchases of foreign bonds by Japanese investors totalled 1.9222 trillion yen in May after net purchases of 2.5783 trillion yen a month earlier, the Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bonds include beneficiary certificates but exclude all bills.</p>
<p>Details of Japanese and foreigners' investments in billions of yen, were as follows:</p>
<p>JAPANESE INVESTMENT</p>
<p> Foreign stocks: Net	     Foreign bonds: Net</p>
<p> May	  + 607.0	     May	  +1922.2</p>
<p> April	+ 391.5	     April	+2578.3</p>
<p>FOREIGNERS' INVESTMENT</p>
<p> Japanese stocks: Net	    Japanese bonds: Net</p>
<p> May	  + 885.2	     May	  +  56.4</p>
<p> April	+ 204.9	     April	+ 237.5</p>
<p>Figures are rounded and based on settlements.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-7587</p>
</text>
